# The built UI bundle. NEVER COMMITTED: it is fetched from the panel's release by fetch-ui.sh, and a
# stale dist/ served in place of the real one looks like "the UI is wrong" rather than "the build is
# wrong".
#
# THE DIRECTORY ITSELF IS NO LONGER IGNORED, only its contents — fetch-ui.sh and README.md live there
# and ARE source. The old rule ignored `cmd/gitdev-ext/ui/*` wholesale, which then also hid the script
# from CI and from the Docker build: both failed with "no such file", which reads as a missing file
# rather than a .gitignore rule that outlived its design.
cmd/gitdev-ext/ui/dist/
cmd/gitdev-ext/ui/.version

ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/

# Built binaries. `go build ./cmd/x` drops the result in the working directory, and an executable
# committed by accident is that many megabytes for everyone who clones afterwards.
#
# `./cmd/e2e-all/<step>` builds to `<step>` in the CURRENT directory, so the e2e helpers need their
# own rules: `bootstrap` and `seed` were each committed once (28MB together) and then stayed in every
# tag, which is why they are listed explicitly rather than covered by the paths above.
/e2e-all
/gitdev-ext
/sweep
/bootstrap
/seed

# Python bytecode from a local run of the log-stream action. The source is log_stream.py; the
# .cpython-313.pyc is an artefact of the interpreter that happened to run it, and it was committed.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
